; Source positions and the reading of them back out of the text they point at.
;
; Below the compiler stages rather than beside them: a span is a location in a
; source file, which CST, SST and everything after them all need, and none of
; them owns it. `span_text` is the shared presentation half, the counterpart of
; `tree_graph` on the span side; the walk over a particular stage's nodes lives
; with that stage.
